PlanTiers compares service plans in one table on a plate: numbered terms down the left, one column per plan, a "Fits when" row and one action per plan, for a buyer choosing a plan tier.

- Data: a `table` block with `"as": "plans"`: `cols` [row label, plan A, plan B, plan C …], `rows` [feature, value per plan]. A row whose label starts "Suits" becomes the "Fits when" row under the table. Every other row is a numbered term row (01, 02 …) in data order, price included.
- `recommend` (column index or plan name) makes that plan the table's one highlight: a `flow-tint` column with a 2 px `flow` line over its name, "Recommended" as a `flow` word (Geist 500 14/20) above the name, and the only primary button; on phones the switcher preselects it and tags its button. Set it only when the page states which plan most clients choose; never pick one to look persuasive. Without it no plan is highlighted, every button is secondary and the switcher preselects the first plan.
- A column named "No plan…" (call-out, pay as you go) is the baseline: `ink-muted` text, no button. Keep it last.
- Action: every plan ends with the page's own CTA (`primary_cta`, its link and `primary_cta_intent`; else `cta.button`), labelled for screen readers with the plan name. No new intents.
- Values: plain values are large (20 px light sans) and centred; a cell holding `[placeholders]` drops to compact 12 px mono (the placeholder keeps its own style at that size), so a draft table still reads as a grid. The "Fits when" label is Geist 500 14/20 `ink-muted`; nothing is uppercase.
- Markup (`blocks/plans.js`): the section's figure is a Plate (`wPlate`, a `line` frame on `surface-raised` with the caption "Aquemi · <nav> · N plans"; it follows the page's theme) holding `.aq-plan-tiers[data-show]` (`has-rec`) > `.aq-plan-tiers__switch` (`role="group"`, `button.aq-plan-tiers__tab[aria-pressed][data-tier]`, `.aq-plan-tiers__tabmark`) and `table.aq-plan-tiers__table`: `thead` (`th.aq-plan-tiers__name` per plan, `.aq-plan-tiers__mark`), `tbody` of `tr.aq-plan-tiers__row` (`th.aq-plan-tiers__label` with `.aq-index`; `td.aq-plan-tiers__c.tN` with `.aq-plan-tiers__cap` and `.aq-plan-tiers__v`), `tbody.aq-plan-tiers__foot` (`tr.aq-plan-tiers__fits`, `tr.aq-plan-tiers__actions`). Cells carry `is-rec` / `is-base`.
- Phones (`@container (max-width: 860px)`): no four stacked tiers. A segmented switcher of real buttons (`radius-sm`, the pressed one `flow-tint` with a 2 px `flow` bottom line) (`aria-pressed`, arrow keys move between them) sets `data-show`; each row shows its numbered label beside the chosen plan's value at a readable size, then "Fits when" and that plan's button. Every plan stays in the DOM: CSS only hides the other columns. Without `data-show` (no script) the switcher hides and every value shows under its row, captioned with its plan.
- Supports `fold: N` and `fold_noun` (first N term rows; "Show all 7 terms"). Put response times and scope first.
- Ground: the section's `surface`, the table on the plate. Keep plans to 2–4 (switcher styles cover up to 6) and cells to one fact. Two routes rather than tiers: Versus. A comparison of things that are not plans you buy: CompareTable.

## Motion

`motion.js`: the plan names drop onto their rule one tier after another, each feature row fills across the tiers (label first, plan by plan), the "Fits when" row follows, then the actions rise and the recommended plan's tab strikes last. Phones: the tier switcher, then the shown plan's rows; pressing a tier slides its values in. Nothing under reduced motion.
